<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christchurch mosque shootings</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christchurch">Christchurch</a> mosque shootings were terrorist attacks on 15 March 2019, when an Australian white supremacist killed 51 people at the Al Noor Mosque and the Linwood Islamic Centre in Christchurch, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>. Within a month <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacinda-ardern">Jacinda Ardern</a>'s government banned most semi-automatic weapons, and in May 2019 New Zealand and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christchurch-call">Christchurch Call</a> against violent extremist content online. The attacker was sentenced to life imprisonment without parole.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christchurch-mosque-shootings.jpg" alt="Christchurch mosque shootings" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michal Klajban · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christchurch_Mosque,_New_Zealand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
